From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <182822903+mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:14:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Spawning: skip impossible mob categories per chunk and reuse
 the spawn state counts (off by default)

entities.spawning.skip-impossible-categories skips the natural spawn attempt
for a mob category when nothing within one chunk can host it (no biome or
structure spawn list for the category, no water for water-only categories).
Those attempts could not spawn anything, so the spawn rate is unchanged; the
random numbers other systems see differ.

entities.spawning.spawn-state-reuse-ticks counts the mobs for natural spawning
only every N ticks and reuses the count plus the spawns since in between.

